        "reason": "This combines three checks (treated as real, figures given, no invented cause). The 'no invented cause' part is the one that tells good runs from bad, and listing possible causes as questions (as this run did) sits close to the line. Grading would be more consistent if the assertion said that naming possible causes as open questions is fine and stating one as fact is not."
      },
      {
        "reason": "No assertion checks the derived figures (percent changes, APAC share of growth, AOV). Here they were all correct, but a run with wrong week-over-week deltas would pass every current check, because the deterministic checks only compare the raw this-week values."
      },
      {
        "reason": "No assertion catches unsupported claims about history. This run says 'in line with the usual flat trend' with only two weeks of data. A broader 'makes no claims beyond the supplied data' check would catch this."
      }
    ],
    "overall": "The single LLM assertion passes clearly. The suite should also check derived figures and flag claims about history the data can't support."
  }
}

